            <ArticleTitle>Afferent neurourology: A novel paradigm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S29-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/nau.20792</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The term &quot;afferent neurourology&quot; is introduced to describe the study of sensory processing related to the genitourinary tract. Urologic disorders that are characterized by abnormal sensory processing are reviewed, and unique challenges to our understanding of these disorders are described. A paradigm which separates afferent urologic disorders from efferent disorders and structural abnormalities is presented.</AbstractText>
